      "writtenOn": "2015-12-10T06:38:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I recommend not introducing command line that takes a password as an argument.  It shows up in history and in the output of ps.\n\nIt\u0027s much better to use a prompt like getpass",
      "revId": "5bb10f75f422544b5192d65ad2b7ae68e956da6f",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a740942_142c4aaa",
        "filename": "keystone/cmd/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-12-10T07:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a case where we might need both forms, as this is also meant to be managed via CMS tools (such as puppet). Ideally this user\u0027s password would be changed or the user would be deleted once keystone is setup.\n\nI\u0027ll need to mull over the best way to address both use-cases elegantly. Remember, this is really only ever to be used for initial setup of keystone not on an ongoing basis (in fact, if this is used outside of bootstrapping, I\u0027d be somewhat worried).",
      "parentUuid": "7a740942_494b1b2c",
      "revId": "5bb10f75f422544b5192d65ad2b7ae68e956da6f",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
